  "details": "# Issue: \n\nWhen doing the typical:\n\n```cs\n\n var players = new VRCPlayerApi[VRCPlayerApi.GetPlayerCount()];  \n\nVRCPlayerApi.GetPlayers(players);\n\n```\n\nThe returned array of players includes players that are currently in the process of leaving. This is noticeable when e.g. creating that array during `OnOwnershipTransferred`.\n\n# Expected Behaviour:\n\nGetting all players should exclude leaving players to prevent problems like trying to make one of them the network owner of an object.\n\n# Additional Information\n\nI've personally ran into this when working on my ownership logic that checks if the new owner is whitelisted and if not tries to move ownership to a whitelisted player. (See attachments)\n\nI've so far worked around this be caching the leaving player in `OnPlayerLeft` and doing a continue inside my loop if they match.",
